course: dictionary
lesson: 8591
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word scoop can be a thing, an amount, an action, or a news story. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Up at the surface, a pelican scoops fish with a stretchy pouch like a net» is about catching food, so scoops is an action.
explain: The word around scoop gives you the clue. «Give me two scoops of ice cream» means an amount, because two tells you how many. «Farmers cut the pods, scoop out the beans» is about taking something out with a spoon-like movement.
explain: When you meet a familiar word in a strange place, do not stop at the first meaning you know. Try each meaning in the sentence. Check which one still makes sense. That is how a sharp reader works.
fact: The same word can have several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: «Scoop» can be a noun (a thing): a tool like a deep spoon, or the amount it holds.
fact: «Scoop» can be a verb (an action): to lift or move something with a scooping movement.
fact: In news, a «scoop» is a story that one newspaper gets before all the others.
fact: Scoop words are used in cooking, science and maths, such as «3 scoops of 25 grams each».
exercise: «Up at the surface, a pelican scoops fish with a stretchy pouch like a net.» What does scoops mean here? | *Lifts up with a sweeping movement | Sleeps on the water | Eats very slowly | Paints the sea blue
exercise: «Sometimes one outlet really gets a true scoop first.» What does scoop mean here? | A spoonful of ice cream | A pet's food bowl | *A news story that one outlet gets before all the others | A tool for digging soil
exercise: A tub has «3 scoops of 25 grams each». How many grams in all? | *75 | 3 | 28 | 100
test:
What is a scoop, as a noun? | *A tool like a deep spoon | A kind of ice cream flavour | A pet's bed | A type of fish
In «she quickly scoops them back in», what kind of word is scoops? | *A verb, an action word | A noun, a thing | An adjective, a describing word | A number
exam:
Which sentence uses scoop as a noun? | *Give me a scoop of rice, please | Scoop the rice into the bowl | She scoops up the rice quickly | Rice is scooped out daily
